+# MEOVV four-image B cutover: source-only local candidate
+
+## Status and scope
+
+Base is live v186 source `f0391481cccd85a4eb53cbe9bf63cdd77d30e350` plus the independently reviewed inspect-only fix `97fb6ab1c2e5303b9e77ec4e52e3762cf912f77a`. This patch enables only the existing four exact member-ID/static-path pairs at the final MEOVV member-detail and PhotoLightbox display points. It changes no `candidatePortrait`, roster helper/WEBP, SOOIN portrait, shared component design, native/editorial image record, score, note, watched state, permission, sharing scope or storage API.
+
+This is a source/test candidate, not a full checkout, complete build, capacity result or deployment. The four source JPEGs remain in Git/public. The original 194 build exclusions and their scripts are unchanged. Compiled pins are deliberately empty: production `--apply` remains fail-closed pending a complete independent build and separate compiled-consumer review. No credentials, HTTP calls, PUT retries, attempt-fence reset, upload or deployment are part of this preparation.
+
+## Evidence, without overstating anonymous verification
+
+The frozen evidence files under `docs/build-assets/` distinguish:
+
+- `meovv-four-owner-readback-original.json`: the unchanged original root report, with `anonymousVerified:false` and `cutover:false` preserved.
+- `meovv-four-owner-readback.json`: fixed four-entry derivative of root's normal owner-browser public-GET image downloads, exact bytes/SHA/decoded geometry, and root's report that each owner PUT occurred once and its server readback verified. The four actual downloaded bodies were independently copied and completely JPEG-decoded locally. MIME is the decoded JPEG file type, not a claim that raw HTTP headers were captured.
+- `meovv-four-anonymous-access.json`: the user's response “可以查看” to the four-image incognito-view request. It binds the original request/reply message IDs and fixed URLs. This confirms anonymous visibility as accepted by root. It **does not** claim anonymous body downloads, SHA/byte measurements, status codes, MIME headers or an automated bypass of the existing Cloudflare block.
+
+The runtime selector binds the two evidence-document SHA values. The local pruner also hashes all three documents and all four saved owner-browser bodies. These hashes preserve reviewed evidence; a handwritten JSON record cannot independently authenticate a browser session, the user's identity or a remote upload. Provenance still relies on the actual preserved conversation/downloads and independent review. The originals and bodies are not old native-image-backup records.
+
+## Consumer and failure behavior
+
+See `meovv-four-consumer-proof.md` and `tests/meovv-build-asset-consumer.test.cjs`.
+
+- Only exact `(member ID, original static path)` pairs map to fixed `/api/build-assets?id=...&version=<SHA>` URLs.
+- Detail and lightbox use the same selected full URL; source/credit/geometry/layout are unchanged.
+- A missing/404/corrupt response or image error leaves the existing error placeholder. Manual retry preserves the exact endpoint, without a cache-buster or fallback to the pruned old JPEG, WEBP, another person or a low-resolution substitute.
+- All five roster WEBPs and SOOIN's full portrait remain unchanged. The generic shared member record uses its existing `/api/media` route.
+- The index keeps its group hero. A failed hero image does not select the portrait-gallery branch. The old portrait metadata remains dormant only while that hero remains present; source and compiled guards pin that branch.
+- Old direct static-image bookmarks are not redirected by this patch and may cease to resolve after pruning. Recovery is via the immutable endpoint or complete rollback package, not an invented static fallback.
+
+The executed proof uses real React SSR and real production component handlers with a declared deterministic hook/ref/portal event model. It is not real browser hydration, focus/layout QA, HTTP/image decoding or deployment verification.
+
+## Exact-four prune gate
+
+`scripts/audit-meovv-build-asset-cutover.mjs` is default read-only. Only explicit `--apply` may unlink exactly the four fixed `PROJECT/dist/client/artist/meovv/*-mnet-profile.jpg` outputs, after all preflight checks pass:
+
+1. Fixed manifest SHA and exactly 25 source guard identities, bytes and SHA; enabled cohort and verified v186 evidence binding.
+2. All runtime source consumers inventoried across app, components, lib, data, hooks, db, vendor and public; exact original-path and dynamic-carrier sets; the nonempty group hero branch.
+3. Exact public originals plus every generated target's bytes/SHA. Target paths reject symlinks and hardlinks; source/public is never a write target.
+4. All three frozen evidence documents and the four actual downloaded response bodies supplied by `--readback-dir`.
+5. Reviewed exact compiled-carrier inventory and byte/SHA pins. Empty/pending pins currently block apply. Pin refresh must not broaden consumer rules or exclusion sets.
+
+All targets are verified again before the first unlink. A preflight error causes zero writes. An operating-system unlink error can be partial; it stops and reports the removed paths, without automatic retry. Reconstruct a fresh complete build from public originals before retrying. There is no R2 write/delete, remote fetch, native record change or arbitrary output-path argument.
+
+After source review and a separately authorized serial full build: independently review exact compiled pins, run read-only dry-run, then apply only the already approved original 194 exclusions and these four. Run the official package helper and `scripts/verify-sites-expanded-archive.py` on the complete gzip stream. A payload estimate is not acceptance; real fulltar headroom must remain at least 2,097,152 bytes. No full build or prune apply on a real dist was run for this source-only candidate.
+
+Example later commands, **only after the preceding review/build gates**:
+
+```sh
+node scripts/audit-meovv-build-asset-cutover.mjs --dry-run --readback-dir /path/to/verified-owner-download-copies
+node scripts/audit-meovv-build-asset-cutover.mjs --apply --readback-dir /path/to/verified-owner-download-copies
+python3 scripts/verify-sites-expanded-archive.py /path/to/official-package.tar.gz
+```
+
+The body directory contains the four fixed `<asset-id>.jpg` filenames recorded in the owner evidence. It is a local evidence input, not an upload source or runtime configuration.
+
+## Recovery and rollback
+
+The offline four-original backup is `meovv-four-originals.tar.gz`, SHA256 `9f8cc1d96285ad06de1d1a4ddfe9178bee2d111e7eee23f7c76d17e37f8b5c7e`. Its isolated restore/full JPEG decode was already tested. Canonical originals also remain in public/Git at the four manifest SHA values.
+
+Fast rollback is the preserved official v186 A-only source-matched package `meovv-A-source-matched-oct22.tar.gz`, SHA256 `f3866d4ba4af3fd26142c167c4c33867be18aec21878e76b6be173d9340e0baa`, with all four static originals retained. The earlier local-only measurement package has SHA256 `e238ec005064cb6687789c0ac3d73b122cc63c2fa8b08cb3470b5176b3cf39e0`; it is not the official package identity. Independent comparison found identical member paths/types/sizes and file-content SHA values, but different tar member mtimes and different expanded tar bytes. Both expanded streams measure 265,717,760 bytes. An alternative is a fresh complete build with B disabled and all four original static outputs restored, followed by normal original-194 pruning and fulltar verification. **Do not merely toggle B off inside an already-pruned package:** that would point consumers at missing files. Disabling the switch makes the four-pruner refuse execution. Remote immutable copies may remain; rollback never overwrites or deletes them.
+
+## Capacity planning, not a measured package result
+
+v186 real fulltar margin was 2,717,696 bytes. Exact removal of the four tar members is estimated to release 6,007,808 bytes, giving 8,725,504 bytes before additions. GENBLUE images 2,467,871 + font 538,732 + WOOAH images 1,391,200 total **4,397,803 bytes**, already including the font. Do not deduct the font twice. That leaves 4,327,701 bytes before new code/licenses and added tar headers/padding. Only the final official complete gzip-expanded stream can prove the >=2 MiB margin.
+
+Any later GENBLUE/WOOAH integration that changes a pinned shared source file requires an exact, independently reviewed pin update preserving the MEOVV branch and fixed-four semantics. This candidate does not include those integrations.
